malware.email:
A file matching the signature of known malware was found on {name}.

{what}

This probably means someone had write access to the site. Until the source is found, changing passwords on its own is not enough.

coreIntegrity.email:
One or more WordPress core files on {name} differ from the official files for that version.

{what}

Core files do not change without a reason. This almost always means something wrote to them.
